  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-f8a99168-7fff-2292-4639-bb36fa79bd31&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear extension, by reason of its unsympathetic scale, bulk, location and detailed design, would result in an overbearing impact,&amp;nbsp; increased sense of enclosure and loss of outlook to the detriment of the living conditions of adjoining residential occupier (255 Kyverdale Road). The proposed development is deemed contrary to policy D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) of the London Plan 2021, policy LP2 (Development and Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed rear extension, by reason of it&#x27;s unsympathetic scale, bulk, location and detailed design, would comprise an incongruous, discordant and overly-prominent form of development, which would detrimentally impact the character and appearance of the site and surrounding area  and also result in the complete loss of rear garden space, to the detriment of the living conditions of residents. As such the proposed development is contrary to policy D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach) of the London Plan 2021, policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033, the Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2025) and the Stamford Hill Area Action Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
